# Editor and IDE state. The project files GoLand writes are one developer's setup —
# window layout, run configurations, the caret's last position — and none of it is part
# of the build: `go build -o bin/mzs ./cmd/mzs` needs nothing but the module.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Build and coverage output, all reproducible from the source. `/mzs` is *not* here:
# that name is the library package's directory now, so the binary has to be built with
# an explicit `-o` and `bin/` is where the docs put it.
/bin/
coverage.out

/ROADMAP.md
